1. Primary Processing Unit: ESP32-WROOM-32U Development BoardDetailed Specifications: Dual-Core 32-bit LX6 Microprocessor operating at $240\text{ MHz}$, $520\text{ KB}$ SRAM, native Hardware PWM output channels, dual UART controllers, and 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converters (ADC).  Engineering Justification:Deterministic Execution: The dual-core architecture allows task separation: Core 0 handles high-speed sensor polling ($250\text{ Hz}$), while Core 1 executes the PID steering and motor speed calculations without timing jitter.U.FL Antenna Connector: The "32U" variant features an IPEX/U.FL external antenna connector, shielding signal lines from electromagnetic interference (EMI) generated by the adjacent brushless motor.2. Front Obstacle Sensor: TF-Luna Micro LiDAR SensorDetailed Specifications: Time-of-Flight (ToF) laser rangefinder, operating distance $0.2\text{ m}$ to $8.0\text{ m}$, update frequency up to $250\text{ Hz}$, $100\text{ Hz}$ default frame rate, UART serial communication ($115,200\text{ baud}$).  Engineering Justification:Long-Range Detection: Ultrasonic sensors fail at high speeds due to narrow echo cone delays, whereas ToF LiDAR updates at $250\text{ Hz}$, giving the vehicle sufficient distance ahead ($8\text{ m}$) to calculate high-speed cornering trajectories.  Immunity to Ambient Light: Operates at $850\text{ nm}$ infrared wavelength, preventing optical noise from indoor arena lighting from disrupting distance readings.3. Side Wall Detection Sensors: Sharp GP2Y0A21YK0F Analog IR Sensors (x2)Detailed Specifications: Infrared triangulation rangefinder, $10\text{ cm}$ to $80\text{ cm}$ detection range, analog output voltage ($0.4\text{ V}$ to $3.1\text{ V}$), update response time $38.3\text{ ms} \pm 9.6\text{ ms}$.  Engineering Justification:Zero Communication Overhead: Outputs an analog voltage read directly via the ESP32’s 12-bit ADC pins (GPIO 34 & GPIO 35), eliminating UART/I2C bus contention.  Short-Range Precision: Highly sensitive at close proximity ($10\text{ cm}\text{--}30\text{ cm}$), providing continuous feedback to center the car between track walls.4. Steering Actuator: DS3218MG High-Torque Digital ServoDetailed Specifications: Operating voltage $4.8\text{ V}\text{--}6.8\text{ V DC}$, stall torque $20\text{ kg}\cdot\text{cm}$ at $6.0\text{ V}$, operating speed $0.14\text{ sec}/60^\circ$, full CNC metal gears, dual ball bearings.  Engineering Justification:Torque Reserve: Standard mini-servos ($1.5\text{ kg}\text{--}3\text{ kg}$) strip plastic gears under aggressive cornering loads or wall contact. The $20\text{ kg}\cdot\text{cm}$ metal gear assembly ensures zero gear stripping and holds precise Ackerman steering angles under lateral acceleration.  5. Main Motor Drive: 60A Sensorless Brushless Electronic Speed Controller (ESC)Detailed Specifications: Continuous current $60\text{ A}$, burst current $320\text{ A}$, input voltage $2\text{S}\text{--}3\text{S}$ LiPo, standard $50\text{ Hz}$ PWM servo signal input ($1500\mu\text{s}$ neutral pulse).  Engineering Justification:Thermal Protection & Headroom: The vehicle draws roughly $10\text{ A}$ on average and $30\text{ A}$ at peak acceleration. A 60A rated ESC operates well within its thermal limits, eliminating overheating or thermal shutdown during prolonged runs.  6. Power Regulation Subsystem: DC-DC Buck Converter (Step-Down)Detailed Specifications: Step-down switching regulator, Input $7.4\text{ V}\text{--}12\text{ V}$, Output $5.0\text{ V DC}$ regulated at up to $3.0\text{ A}$ continuous output.  Engineering Justification:Separation of Power Rails: Isolates logic components ($5\text{ V}$) from motor voltage sag ($7.4\text{ V}$). Linear regulators (e.g., LM7805) waste excess voltage as heat, whereas switching buck regulators operate at $>90\%$ efficiency, keeping logic power clean and stable.  7. Safety Mechanisms: Master Power Switch & E-Stop ButtonDetailed Specifications:ON/OFF Switch: Heavy-duty inline toggle switch rated for $12\text{ V} / 20\text{ A}$.  E-Stop Switch: Latching red mushroom-head push button wired between GPIO 23 and GND
